NCMAT v7
#
# Test file with an unusual VDOS, not intended for physics usage.
#
# Provenance:
#
#   The file tsl-ortho-D_19K.ncmat from the Liquids plugin by D. DiJulio and
#   J. I. Marquez Damian (https://github.com/dddijulio/ncrystal-plugin-
#   Liquids, commit 308f623). Only the VDOS was kept, written with up to 7
#   significant digits.
#
#   According to the original file, the input data was taken from the TSL
#   library in: G.P.A. Nobre et al., "ENDF/B-VIII.1: Updated Nuclear Reaction
#   Data Library for Science and Applications", Nuclear Data Sheets, 210, 1,
#   (2026), https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nds.2026.04.001
#
# Why it is a test case:
#
#   Similar to vdos_paraH2.ncmat, but for a heavier atom and with the
#   oscillator peak at a lower energy (0.387eV, 4 points wide). More than 2300
#   of the 2806 points are exactly zero, and the values include subnormal
#   numbers (down to 1.3e-310).
#
@DENSITY
  0.17399 g_per_cm3
@DYNINFO
  element  D
  fraction 1
  type     vdos
